Place a cursor in the rows pushed above a split line

0010 splits a line too tall for the room left above it, pushing every
row above it to the scrollback and ending the reflow there. Ending it
also passed by the check after the loop that puts a cursor which went
off the top at row 0, so with the cursor in those rows -- homed by a
program, or restored on leaving the alternate screen -- it got no
position and the process aborted ("screen_resize failed to update
cursor position"). Found by fuzzing BeerSSH's emulator; every seed
reached it within seconds.

Place such a cursor where that check would: row 0, its column clamped.

--- a/src/screen.c
+++ b/src/screen.c
@@ -799,6 +799,15 @@
         for(int row = 0; row < old_row_start; row++)
           sb_pushline_from_buffer(screen, old_buffer, row, old_cols, old_lineinfo[row].continuation);
 
+      /* A cursor in the rows pushed above goes to the top, as one that
+       * moves off the top always has: the check after the loop that
+       * does that is passed by, since this ends the loop. Missed, the
+       * cursor had no position and the process aborted. */
+      if(old_cursor.row < old_row_start && new_cursor.row == -1) {
+        new_cursor.row = 0;
+        new_cursor.col = old_cursor.col < new_cols ? old_cursor.col : new_cols - 1;
+      }
+
       for(int head = 0; head < -new_row_start; head++) {
         int count = reflow_take(old_buffer, cells, offset, line_width, new_cols);
 
